#import "release.typ": release, plain-words, signing
#show: release.with(
  title: "Cat Surrender (Owner Relinquishment) Agreement",
  intro: [*We know this can be a hard decision, and we're grateful you came to us.* This is the agreement between you and Sun Brewed Homestead Inc. ("the Homestead") and its Kiki's Cat Club rescue program for surrendering the cat below. Please read all of it and ask us about anything unclear before you sign. Below, "I" means you.],
  note: [Signed electronically. The signer must be 18 or older.],
  details: ("Cat's name and description", "Known health or behavior issues (or \"none\")"),
)

#plain-words[
- The cat becomes ours for good. We'll care for it and look for a loving home, but we can't promise when.
- Please tell us everything you know, especially any bites. It keeps people and animals safe.
- After signing you can't reclaim the cat or learn where it goes.
]

*1. Ownership.* I am the cat's legal owner, or am authorized by its owner, and I have the right to surrender it. No one else has a claim to the cat.

*2. Transfer of all rights.* I give up all ownership and rights to the cat, permanently. From signing, the Homestead may decide everything about its care, including veterinary treatment, spaying or neutering, vaccination, fostering, adoption to a new home it chooses, or, only if a veterinarian advises that it is necessary to end suffering, humane euthanasia. I cannot reclaim the cat or be told where it goes.

*3. Honest history.* I have told the Homestead everything I know about the cat's age, health, vaccinations, temperament and history, including every time it has bitten or seriously scratched anyone, and especially any bite in the last 14 days (a recent bite may require a rabies quarantine), and have given it any medical records I have. I understand the Homestead relies on this to keep people and animals safe.

*4. No guarantee of placement.* I understand the Homestead is a small rescue with limited space and cannot promise the cat will be adopted, or by when.

*5. Donation.* Any surrender donation I make helps with the cat's care. It is voluntary and not refundable.

*6. Release and indemnity.* I release the Homestead, its directors, officers, volunteers, members and agents from claims about the cat's care, placement and, as described above, euthanasia, to the fullest extent the law allows. I agree to indemnify them against claims arising from information I gave that was false or incomplete, or from anyone else's claim to own the cat.

#signing[*7. General.* This agreement is governed by California law. If any part is held unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. I agree to sign electronically, and my electronic signature binds me as if written by hand. *I am at least 18. I have read this agreement and had the chance to ask questions about it, and I sign it voluntarily.*]
